<title>GERMANY: Victoria 96 gp net profit rises to 116 bln.</title>
<headline>Victoria 96 gp net profit rises to 116 bln.</headline>
<text>
<p>DUESSELDORF, Germany, June 4 Reuter - Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   116     vs 86</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     276     vs 205</p>
<p>    Group premium income		     9,578   vs 9,300</p>
<p>    Total claims				 5,780   vs 5,905</p>
<p>Group underwriting profit</p>
<p>    (before claims equalisation reserve) 34	vs 23</p>
<p>    Capital investments			40,977  vs 37,162</p>
<p>    Revenue from capital investments     2,789   vs 2,657</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share		 51	vs 45 marks</p>
<p>    Employees				    10,307  vs 10,759</p>
<p>    Dividend				     28	vs 25 percent</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German insurer is Victoria Versicherungs-Gruppe AG.</p>
</text>
